<title>BELGIUM: G-BANK, NMKN/SNCI CUT SAVINGS CERTS RATES.</title>
<headline>G-BANK, NMKN/SNCI CUT SAVINGS CERTS RATES.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's Generale Bank</p>
<p>and Credit a L'Industrie (NMKN/SNCI) said on</p>
<p>Tuesday they cut cut interest rates on their bank savings</p>
<p>certificates, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Generale Bank</p>
<p>    MATURITY	   NEW RATE	OLD RATE</p>
<p>    one year	   2.80 pct	 3.00 pct</p>
<p>    two years	  3.30 pct	 3.50 pct</p>
<p>    three years	3.80 pct	 4.10 pct</p>
<p>    five years	 4.70 pct	 5.00 pct</p>
<p>Credit a L'Industrie</p>
<p>    MATURITY	  NEW RATE	OLD RATE</p>
<p>    one year	  2.80 pct	 3.00 pct</p>
<p>    two years	 3.30 pct	 3.50 pct</p>
<p>    three years     3.75 pct	 4.00 pct</p>
<p>    five years	4.60 pct	 4.90 pct</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
